    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d180">

                <pb facs="0182" n="170" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg170"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to the British Prime Minister</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Churchill</hi>)<anchor n="68" xml:id="d180-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-12-26">26 December 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>680. Replying to your 858, I have asked our Ambassador to call upon you as soon
                    as possible and I am ready to be of all assistance I can in this difficult
                    situation.</p>
                <p>I hope that your presence there on the spot will result in achieving an entirely
                    satisfactory solution.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Roosevelt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d180-f1" n="68" type="source" xml:id="d180-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram sent to the Ambassador in Greece for delivery to Prime Minister
                    Churchill. Copy obtained from the Franklin D. Roosevelt Library, Hyde Park,
                    N.Y.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
